--- PARITY (web/src/components/data-display/format/Distance.tsx) ---
Pure unit-aware readout. A finite `miles` wins, else a finite `km` (web if/else-if); the value is normalised
to SI metres (miles*1609.344 / km*1000), converted to the user's distance preference via the shared
UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi (web convertDistanceFromSI), and formatted through the golden-verified
ScalarFormatters.FormatNumber (web fmtNumber: en-US grouping + fixed fraction digits), rendering "{number} {unit}".
Precision resolves prop ?? preference ?? 2 (the web fmtNumber _globalPrecision default). The raw caller value is
shown at two decimals in its ORIGINAL unit through the WinUI ToolTip (web title attribute). No finite input ->
the em dash (web <span>—</span>). The only data source is the synchronous unit preference (P1/S8 IDistanceUnitsSource,
the useUnits analogue), so — like accepted presentational predecessors AnimatedNumber/VisuallyHidden — there is
no loading/error/stale/offline chrome; the reproduced branches are the formatted-value readout and the no-value
em dash across the mi/km channels and the distance-unit (mi/km/ft) + precision variants. Surface declares no
localizable English strings (unit labels come from the Core UnitLabels registry; the dash is the shared
UnitFormatters.DefaultEmptyDisplay). Diagnostics: view.opened slug=Distance (slug only; never the value).

